cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or data, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Code and data for: Value-based and regulation-aware placement of sectionalizing switches, reclosers, and tie switches in distribution networks with AC-feasible two-stage restoration"
version: 1.0.0
license: MIT
authors:
  - family-names: Yudiansyah
    given-names: Hafizh Agus
    affiliation: "Department of Electrical Engineering, Institut Teknologi Sepuluh Nopember, Surabaya, Indonesia"
  - family-names: Wibowo
    given-names: Rony Seto
    affiliation: "Department of Electrical Engineering, Institut Teknologi Sepuluh Nopember, Surabaya, Indonesia"
  - family-names: Wardana
    given-names: Harjuan Aditya
    affiliation: "Department of Electrical Engineering, Institut Teknologi Sepuluh Nopember, Surabaya, Indonesia"
abstract: >-
  Exact evaluator and optimization experiments for the placement of manual
  switches, remote-controlled switches, reclosers and tie switches in
  distribution networks. The evaluator combines failure mode and effect
  analysis, two-stage restoration with AC feasibility at four load levels,
  the expected customer interruption cost and the guaranteed-service
  compensation of Indonesian regulation. The repository contains the data of
  the IEEE 33-bus, IEEE 69-bus, RBTS Bus 2 and Bawean (Indonesia) systems, the
  results reported in the article and the scripts that reproduce its figures
  and tables.
keywords:
  - distribution system reliability
  - switch placement
  - service restoration
  - customer interruption cost
  - regulatory compensation
  - multi-objective optimization
